{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.21230429","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.21230429","prefix":"10.5281","suffix":"zenodo.21230429","identifiers":[],"alternateIdentifiers":[],"creators":[{"name":"Novickis, Alexander","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Alexander","familyName":"Novickis","affiliation":["Independent Researcher"],"nameIdentifiers":[{"nameIdentifier":"0009-0004-2618-006X","nameIdentifierScheme":"ORCID"}]}],"titles":[{"title":"Inline Hardware KV-Cache Compression for Long-Context Transformer Inference: An Architectural Case for a Memory-Path Compression Engine"}],"publisher":"Zenodo","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"subject":"KV cache"},{"subject":"KV-cache compression"},{"subject":"long-context inference"},{"subject":"transformer inference"},{"subject":"LLM inference"},{"subject":"batch-1 decode"},{"subject":"memory bandwidth"},{"subject":"memory wall"},{"subject":"quantization"},{"subject":"INT4"},{"subject":"INT8"},{"subject":"entropy coding"},{"subject":"recency"},{"subject":"near-memory computing"},{"subject":"compute-in-memory"},{"subject":"soft-IP"},{"subject":"AXI4"},{"subject":"LPDDR5"},{"subject":"HBM"},{"subject":"functional safety"},{"subject":"ISO 26262"},{"subject":"ml"},{"subject":"hardware"},{"subject":"architecture"},{"subject":"inference"},{"subject":"soft-ip"},{"subject":"kv-cache"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-07-07","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"arXiv:1706.03762","relatedIdentifierType":"arXiv"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"arXiv:2211.05102","relatedIdentifierType":"arXiv"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.1145/1498765.1498785","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"arXiv:2305.13245","relatedIdentifierType":"arXiv"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"arXiv:2402.02750","relatedIdentifierType":"arXiv"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"arXiv:2401.18079","relatedIdentifierType":"arXiv"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"arXiv:2403.05527","relatedIdentifierType":"arXiv"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.20669977","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"HasVersion","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.21230434","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"HasVersion","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.21230430","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"v2","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Autoregressive transformer inference at long context length is bound not by arithmetic throughput but by the bandwidth and capacity required to stream the key/value (KV) cache from external memory on every generated token. Software KV-cache quantization mitigates this but spends the accelerator's own compute and bandwidth to do so. This paper makes the architectural case for an alternative: a small, fixed-function, protocol-agnostic hardware compression engine placed inline on the memory datapath, which quantizes and entropy-codes KV blocks on eviction and reconstructs them on fetch, at memory line rate and at zero cost to accelerator FLOPs. We frame the KV-cache bottleneck quantitatively, position memory-path hardware compression against software quantization and near-memory/compute-in-memory approaches, and describe — at the block level — a recency-aware engine that compresses distant tokens more aggressively than recent ones while presenting a transparent read/write interface to the host accelerator. We discuss integration (an AXI/memory-boundary drop-in with a first-class bypass mode), a functional-safety-instrumented variant suitable for automotive and industrial edge inference, and the honest limits of the approach. This is a positioning and architectural paper; detailed microarchitecture and quantitative sign-off data are shared under a mutual non-disclosure agreement.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21230429","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":2,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":2,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":3,"versionOfCount":1,"created":"2026-07-07T01:01:21.000Z","registered":"2026-07-07T01:01:21.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-08-27T16:12:49.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"cern.zenodo","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"cern","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.21230429","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.20669977","type":"dois"},{"id":"10.1145/1498765.1498785","type":"dois"}]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.21230430","type":"dois"},{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.21230429","type":"dois"},{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.21230434","type":"dois"}]},"versionOf":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.21230429","type":"dois"}]}}}}